# text = " My replies informed the doctor , in the first place , that I had so managed matters at Thorpe Ambrose as to produce a general impression that Armadale intended to marry me ; in the second place , that my husband's early life had not been of a kind to exhibit him favorably in the eyes of the world ; in the third place , that we had been married , without any witnesses present who knew us , at a large parish church in which two other couples had been married the same morning , to say nothing of the dozens on dozens of other couples ( confusing all remembrance of us in the minds of the officiating people ) who had been married since .
